idarity that is ignored or underplayed by theories of power or self-interest--are at the heart of this novel inquiry into the meeting place between normative theories of what we think we should do and empirical studies of who we actually are. Solidarity, Alexander demonstrates, creates inclusive and exclusive social structures and shows how they can be repaired. It is not perfect, it is not absolute, and the horrors which occur in its lapses have been seen all too frequently in the forms of discrimination, genocide, and war. Despite its worldly flaws and contradictions, however, solidarity and the project of civil society remain our best hope: the antidote to every divisive institution, every unfair distribution, every abusive and dominating hierarchy. This grand, sweeping statement and rigorous empirical investigation is a major contribution to our thinking about the real but ideal world in which we all reside.","displaySummary":"This grand, sweeping statement and rigorous empirical investigation is a major contribution to our thinking about the real but ideal world in which we all reside.","primaryTopic":"Genocide, Atrocity & Political Violence","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Society & Culture","confidence":"high","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Society & Culture","score":8,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"llm_classifier","rawLabel":"Society & Culture","mappedSubject":"Society & Culture","score":8,"confidence":"high","note":"The book primarily explores concepts of civil society, which falls under Society & Culture, while also addressing political elements inherent in those discussions.","id":"subject-evidence-book-the-civil-sphere-jeffrey-c-alexander-1"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"Pluralism (Social sciences)","mappedSubject":"Society & Culture","score":5,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-open-library-the-civil-sphere-jeffrey-c-alexander","id":"subject-evidence-book-the-civil-sphere-